    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/crdm/crdm-requirements-workflow.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "BPMN reference",
      "prov:value": "**Nothing about running it changes.** Step ids are unchanged, so\n`workflow_complete` still takes `A_Implement`, `A_Close`, `BA_Signoff` by name;\nthe interpreter enters a phase by itself and `workflow_next` tells you which one\nyou are in (`inside: Phase 6 Implement + acceptance`)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/crdm/crdm-requirements-workflow.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "BPMN reference",
      "prov:value": "**Phase 6 is one subprocess and not three** because the loops say so: a rejected\nincrement, an MVP that is not ready, and stakeholder findings all route back into\nimplementation. A subprocess has one exit and cannot be re-entered once finished,\nso splitting that region would have changed what the diagram says."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/crdm/crdm-requirements-workflow.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Phase 3 — Requirements definition",
      "prov:value": "Record \"N/A — no rendered surface\" in the\n   template otherwise. Owner, 2026-09-23 ([`wiregen`](../../../methodologies/wiregen.md)):\n   *\"wireframe is part of design process for adjudication\"*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/crdm/crdm-requirements-workflow.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Consumer burden is a requirement, not a nicety (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "The standing rule, from the repository owner: *a downstream consumer must never\nhave to string-manipulate, re-derive, or assume a rule in order to use what we\npublish.* If an artefact makes a consumer parse a name, strip a prefix,\nsubstitute a base URL, or know a convention that is written down only in prose,\nthe requirement is not met."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/crdm/crdm-requirements-workflow.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "Phase 5 — Sign-off and bean creation",
      "prov:value": "**Post sign-off summary** on the issue — what was agreed, what was deferred\n   — **and record it.** `BA_Signoff` is an adjudication (issue #2405, FR-013):\n   the BA answers `approve`, `amend`, `reject`, `defer` or `cancel`, and\n   `A_RecordSignoff` appends a `requirement-signoff` attestation for the\n   requirement set (who, when, scope, outcome, the stage it moves the set to,\n   the reason, and the permalink to the issue comment).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#2405",
        "FR-013"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/crdm/crdm-requirements-workflow.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The agreed set is an ASSET, and Phase 5 is where it gets a home",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-09-21, on a run where this step had been reached and the offer left\n`docs/` out of it:\n\n> this is a memory asset as part of design, so it goes into docs/ […] if it is\n> realated to some harness/feature/tool that detailed infromation/design/\n> planning/etc go into that harness' docs/\n\n**Requirements are produced while BUILDING, and they are not the thing built.**\nWithout this step they end as an issue and a conversation — which is how the\noutput of the process that exists to produce durable requirements becomes the\none thing the knowledge graph never learns.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/crdm/crdm-requirements-workflow.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "A harness feature's documents: proposed in `docs/proposals/`, filed in `docs/requirements/` (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-09-23 (issue #1164): when the feature is **the harness's own**, the\ndocuments this process produces (initial analysis, MVP, the options, the\nagreed requirements) **live and are updated under `docs/`**, in two declared\nsub-graphs of it.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1164",
        "2026-09-23"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-23"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/crdm/crdm-requirements-workflow.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "A harness feature's documents: proposed in `docs/proposals/`, filed in `docs/requirements/` (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "**The directory says what KIND of document it is; the stage is a field**\n(issue #2405, FR-010). The requirements document is a `RequirementSet`\nwhose `stage` (`draft` … `accepted`, or `rejected`, `cancelled`,\n`superseded`) is recorded in the set and moved only by a recorded sign-off.\nThe directory follows the stage — a set reaching `accepted` is when its\nproposal is filed — but it no longer stands in for it: before this, \"where the\nfile is\" was the only record of a decision, and nothing said who made it.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#2405",
        "FR-010"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/crdm/crdm-requirements-workflow.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "A harness feature's documents: proposed in `docs/proposals/`, filed in `docs/requirements/` (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "- The assessment of open requirements standards is in [`methodologies/requirements-standards-assessment.md`](../../../methodologies/requirements-standards-assessment.md) (bean `folio-assistant-1gf7`), and the literature search, adopted/rejected methodologies, and proposed BPMN filing workflow (`Process_RequirementsFiling`, [`sdlc/processes/requirements-filing.bpmn`](../../processes/requirements-filing.bpmn)) are in [`methodologies/requirements-filing-and-organisation.md`](../../../methodologies/requirements-filing-and-organisation.md) and [`docs/proposals/requirements-filing-organisation.md`](../../../docs/proposals/requirements-filing-organisation.md) (bean `folio-assistant-qh1s`, issue #1164).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean folio-assistant-1gf7",
        "bean folio-assistant-qh1s",
        "#1164",
        "docs/proposals/requirements-filing-organisation.md"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/crdm/crdm-requirements-workflow.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Phase 6 — Iterative development",
      "prov:value": "9. **Staging cleanup** — **a merged PR's preview goes away on its own**\n   (owner, 2026-09-20): the merge is the confirmation, since the main site\n   now shows the same thing.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/crdm/crdm-requirements-workflow.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Theme and UI review is NOT a Phase 6 step — it happens at ingestion",
      "prov:value": "This section used to put [`theme-ui-review`](../../../skills/ui/ui-core/theme-ui-review.md)\non the single edge out of MVP acceptance in `crdm-deliver.bpmn`. **That call was\nremoved on 2026-09-24.** The owner ruled that theme review happens *\"at\ningestion of graphical assets in context of website or app design\"*, and, asked\nwhether that meant only there: *\"Yes only at ingestion\"* (bean `9fdi`).\n\nSo `GW_StakeholderOK`'s `accepted` branch now closes the phase directly. The\nreview runs when the graphical assets arrive, from `ingest-theme.bpmn`, where a\nfinding is a decision about what the assets will be rather than a defect in\nsomething that shipped. If you are looking for where accessibility, branding and\nlocales get checked for a UI, look there — not here.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 9fdi",
        "2026-09-24"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-24"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/crdm/crdm-requirements-workflow.md#provenance-12",
